  "title": "Investigating the Contribution of Socio-Physical Structure of Neighborhoods on Residents' Sense of Attachment",
  "authors": "Navid KHALEGHIMOGHADDAM et al., 2023",
  "research_question": "1. To what extent do the social and physical factors contribute to residents' satisfaction with their neighborhoods?\n2. Which of the social and physical factors plays the more significant role in creating an attachment to the neighborhood?",
  "design_type": "cross_sectional",
  "participants": {
    "n": 180,
    "description": "180 residents (93 men, 87 women, mean age=35 years) from 4 neighborhoods in Karaj, Iran. Each neighborhood had n=45 participants. Most owned their homes (68.75%) and had a master's degree (47.5%).",
    "recruitment": "Randomly selected using a cluster sampling method, volunteered to participate through door-to-door visits."
  },
